# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this the tree's line endings follow whoever cloned it: git on
# Windows checked these files out as CRLF and quietly normalised them back to
# LF on commit, so the mismatch was invisible until the same tree was opened
# on Linux, where nothing normalises and every CRLF file read as fully
# modified. Committing the rule removes the platform from the question.
* text=auto eol=lf
